  "pli-tv-kd7:12.1.1": "“Whose meditation is going well” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>phāsuvihārika</i>. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vihāra</i> is a common Sutta term for a state of meditation, as in <i lang='pi' translate='no'>diṭṭhadhammasukhavihāra</i>, “a happy (meditation) abiding in this very life”, which is a reference to the four absorptions. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Phāsu</i> means “comfortable” or “at ease”. Although this may be understood quite broadly, it seems likely that meditation would be the main connotation. ",
